{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves","id":1485220,"title":"Blood Cauldron on werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-28T15:59:06-07:00","id":1485220,"title":"Blood Cauldron on werewolves","content":"The real question us how blood cauldron is working when the target can soak agg damage?<br /> <br /> First hypothesis the blood is actually boiling but the body of the character, may be it a werewolf or a vampire with fortitude, resist the burn. However the victim still lose his blood. According to V20 a wounded character lose 1 blood point per health level checked, so a werewolf soaking the agg damage would just convert them into unsoakable lethal damage du to the blood loss like an hemorrhage<br /> <br /> Second hypothesis the blood is not boiling at all thanks to it's supernatural resistance, so fortitude or werewolves stamina in other form than their natural can completely protect them against blood cauldron<br /> <br /> The description of blood cauldron make me think that the answer is in the second hypothesis, especially with the exemple of the ghoul surviving it by soaking ALL damage with fortitude<br /> <br /> Also does the rank 1 homid gift master of fire working on the blood cauldron? My friend argue me that's it's not the same burn as a fire because it's a liquid","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-28-2022, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T17:09:05-07:00","id":1485232,"title":"","content":"Due to crossover weirdness a Werewolf has much more blood points than a human. So if you are in a form that can soak it, you're probably going to be fine. Even if you don't soak it, the blood loss isn't in addition to the levels of damage it's the consequence of damage. That pretty much only applies to Vampiric biology, as a normal human will just be dead, and a supernatural will be very pissed off with 3-5 Levels of Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> And Master of Fire is about Fire. It can help you with the Path of Flames, but won't do much against Path of Blood, which is essentially about touching someone to make the blood in their veins cook on touch - there may be heat from the reaction, but there is no fire, it's just magical blood of the vampire causing a change in the temperature of the blood in the touched target.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T20:02:51-07:00","id":1485248,"title":"","content":"Werewolves can\u2019t soak Cauldron of Blood. Only Fortitude can soak it. Aside from that unsoakable aggravated damage, I probably wouldn\u2019t bother with additional effects of blood loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T22:01:23-07:00","id":1485256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485248#post1485248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves can\u2019t soak Cauldron of Blood. Only Fortitude can soak it. Aside from that unsoakable aggravated damage, I probably wouldn\u2019t bother with additional effects of blood loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natural agg soak for Garou counts as &quot;a power like Fortitude&quot; for so many vampire powers that it seems pointless to try and bring the wording up as a precedent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T01:51:26-07:00","id":1485268,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help guys ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T03:14:51-07:00","id":1485270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485256#post1485256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Natural agg soak for Garou counts as &quot;a power like Fortitude&quot; for so many vampire powers that it seems pointless to try and bring the wording up as a precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Thanks Dino. Vampire doesn't have anyone NATURALLY soaking most forms of Aggravated damage, and this would pretty much count as soakable for Garou (as long as they are not in their breed form).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 06-29-2022, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T06:44:30-07:00","id":1485282,"title":"","content":"Or their breed form is Crinos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T07:01:33-07:00","id":1485283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485256#post1485256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Natural agg soak for Garou counts as &quot;a power like Fortitude&quot; for so many vampire powers that it seems pointless to try and bring the wording up as a precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were the case, the power only had to say that it causes aggravated damage, as numerous other powers do. It doesn\u2019t say that though, it says that the damage is aggravated and that it can only be soaked by Fortitude. If you want to house rule it, you can do so, but the rules do state specifically that it requires Fortitude to soak. <br /> <br /> Touching a werewolf is nearly suicidal anyway, no reason to make the power so ineffective on top of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T07:45:47-07:00","id":1485289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485283#post1485283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that were the case, the power only had to say that it causes aggravated damage, as numerous other powers do. It doesn\u2019t say that though, it says that the damage is aggravated and that it can only be soaked by Fortitude. If you want to house rule it, you can do so, but the rules do state specifically that it requires Fortitude to soak.<br /> <br /> Touching a werewolf is nearly suicidal anyway, no reason to make the power so ineffective on top of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. The power is written from the perspective of Vampire addressing only what happens with vampires and mortals if you touch them. Of course there is no soaking aggravated in Vampire unless you have Fortitude or say Serpentis. However, Werewolf is pretty specific that Garou soak aggravated damage with their Stamina.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T09:56:16-07:00","id":1485297,"title":"","content":"Vampire rules clearly state on V20 page 278: Consider all damage \u2014 bashing, lethal, and aggravated \u2014 to be soakable with the werewolf\u2019s normal Stamina.<br /> Still, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> might have a case. The write-up of the power in V20 states only Fortitude allows to soak, so fringe powers like visceratika's Armor of Terra, are excluded from the soak.<br /> Strangely enough the example lupines in the book have Stamina, but rarely fortitude - despite the being able to soak aggravated damage with Stamina.<br /> <br /> So, we can only guess if this is intentional or not.<br /> The argument, that the power is written from the POV of a vampire game and &quot;only Fortitude&quot; is meant to mean &quot;only means of soaking aggravated damage&quot; (which is, in practice only Fortitude) has merit, but so does the argument, that the V20 book has other powers that allow to soak agg, especially lupine stamina, and that these might be excluded here on purpose.<br /> <br /> In the end, the ST will have to make a judgment call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T10:03:09-07:00","id":1485298,"title":"","content":"I agree with Asmodai, W20 is very clear about it, werewolves's stamina can soak every damage, including aggravated. The only exception is silver, some specific gifts and powers of other supernatural beings (like the level 9 chimestry Mayaparisatya) and their breed form. When the garou is a metis he keep all his ability including regen and soak in all their form, but they are never protected against silver and suffer a physical or psychological deformity.<br /> <br /> The point is that each game are made to be played without crossing with the other, so i understand your confusion about it. Plus even in their breed form Werewolves have a hell of a powerfull vitality, they can heal in a few days a wound that would heal in a few month for humans, and they will never suffer any scar or permanent injury after that (except if they roll rage to survive death)<br /> Werewolves in WOD are litterally made for battle, for war, and against monsters far deadlier than large majority of vampires, so it's not surprising that they are feared even by the oldest leeches of the night","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-29-2022, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T10:52:38-07:00","id":1485301,"title":"","content":"I have a friend who ST werewolf and he rules that in the breed form 1 success is enough to kill (naturally, unless the werewolf is a metis). I think his treatment is a bit harsh. I think that, as specified by the rules, for every blood lost it causes an unsoakable lethal damage from blood loss, besides the aggravated from the successes, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T10:59:43-07:00","id":1485302,"title":"","content":"Again, the blood loss is meant for Vampires to map the fact that the blood in their blood pool is being destroyed, not for normal humans. Normal humans are dead from their blood cooking them from the inside, bloodloss is irrelevant.. However none of the splats are &quot;normal humans&quot;, they will take a shitload of damage in breed from, but it won't insta kill them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T13:05:41-07:00","id":1485310,"title":"","content":"Okay, book time. Feral Claws has the same wording about soaking agg, at least in Revised, and what the W:tA Revised Storyteller's Handbook has to say about that on page 197 is exactly what I posted up thread. Furthermore, Cauldron of Blood halves the damage that it does to Garou and Fera, because of the super-high Blood capacity for shapechangers - so one level per two points boiled. It's a terrible power to try and use against Garou, quite honestly. You're better off just getting Celerity - though whether that's to attack or to run away at super speed, I leave up to the player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T06:04:46-07:00","id":1485360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485310#post1485310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, book time. Feral Claws has the same wording about soaking agg, at least in Revised, and what the W:tA Revised Storyteller's Handbook has to say about that on page 197 is exactly what I posted up thread. Furthermore, Cauldron of Blood halves the damage that it does to Garou and Fera, because of the super-high Blood capacity for shapechangers - so one level per two points boiled. It's a terrible power to try and use against Garou, quite honestly. You're better off just getting Celerity - though whether that's to attack or to run away at super speed, I leave up to the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fact it may be a change between 2 edition, but in my v20 book in antagonist section, page 386 they state that a garou have 10 blood points in their veins, they are just very powerfull and count as double<br /> So 10 blood point drank give 20 vitae to the vampire who drink it. In that case 2 success to inflict 1 agg damage isn't right since it's just the power of the lupin's blood that double the benefits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 06-30-2022, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T07:21:47-07:00","id":1485369,"title":"","content":"Saur Ops Specialist is referring to the official crossover rules Vampire/Werewolf as printed in the Storyteller Handbook. You'll note that those were not reprinted in V20, so we have to go back to Revised for those rulings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T23:11:36-07:00","id":1485455,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t agree with the argument that werewolves can soak Cauldron of Blood, but I can at least see the logic in it. Requiring two successes for every level of damage inflicted, however, is so absurd that it boggles my mind. I know that one of the books says it, but I have no hesitation to throw out something in one of the books if it\u2019s completely ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T07:16:07-07:00","id":1485503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485455#post1485455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t agree with the argument that werewolves can soak Cauldron of Blood, but I can at least see the logic in it. Requiring two successes for every level of damage inflicted, however, is so absurd that it boggles my mind. I know that one of the books says it, but I have no hesitation to throw out something in one of the books if it\u2019s completely ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get into fights with the union of flesh and spirit at your own risk, and don't expect them to drop - or even feel pain - from the same things that could cripple or kill kine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T09:58:40-07:00","id":1485515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485455#post1485455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t agree with the argument that werewolves can soak Cauldron of Blood, but I can at least see the logic in it. Requiring two successes for every level of damage inflicted, however, is so absurd that it boggles my mind. I know that one of the books says it, but I have no hesitation to throw out something in one of the books if it\u2019s completely ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my memory's correct a single werewolf (a silent strider) killed the founder of the setites clan, and before dying the vampire cursed him and his tribe to never be able to put a foot on their homeland again. Of course not all werewolves are capable of such a feat but even without talking about any gift a clan founder have some powers that very few can imagine, way more powerfull than blood cauldron, so they're certainly extremely resistant.<br /> In my opinion, yes, they totally can soak the damage of that power<br /> However as ST you can do wathever you want if it suits you for your story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 07-01-2022, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:38:30-07:00","id":1485533,"title":"","content":"I believe the werewolf that tried to kill the Setites clan founder was backed by an attack force. Also I think, they can't get rest in their homeland, but can enter it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T12:44:57-07:00","id":1485535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485220-blood-cauldron-on-werewolves?p=1485533#post1485533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the werewolf that tried to kill the Setites clan founder was backed by an attack force. Also I think, they can't get rest in their homeland, but can enter it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making a clan founder afraid for their existence is still pretty nice. The terms also prevent them from regaining Gnosis without catching the attention of some evil spirits, at least as far as Rage Across Egypt had it.<br /> <br /> (Crinos alone is on par with an 8 or 9-dot power from Protean or Serpentis to gain a battle form, I forget the specifics; it maps pretty closely with the stat boosts and secondary powers, like vastly improved resilience.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-03T16:31:08-07:00","id":1485729,"title":"","content":"Not only the clan founders, i've read somewhere some of the law of the first Enoch from Cain itself, warning his descendants against werewolf (a piece of the Book of Nod maybe, can't remember)<br /> If Cain himself, the first Vampire, an undead god was afraid of them, it's for a damn good reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:00:35-07:00","id":1486167,"title":"","content":"If you have Thaum 5 and you wanna kill a Werewolf, you're better off using Thaum 4 and hoping for enough successes to have them fall unconscious. Whether rage lets them regen blood or not will fall into crossover arbitration of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}